/Title (logistics tracking: a configurable data model, record-level security, workflow automation, reporting, and an application framework. Building on Salesforce means that authentication, sharing, audit trail, reporting, and user interface components are provided by the platform rather than being re-implemented. This allows the project to concentrate on the logistics-specific parts: the parcel schema, the tracking prompt, the retrieval flow, and the conversational agent. The Developer Edition provides a no-cost environment that includes Prompt Builder, Flow Builder, Agent Builder, and Apex, which makes it suitable for an academic prototype.)
